  "report_period": "Week 47 (17th Nov to 24th Nov 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Following the acquisition of the Capesize \"Chow\" 181/2016 SWS, China (SS 09/2026, DD 12/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted), clients of Genco Shipping have purchased the sister vessel \"Comanche\" 180/2016 SWS, China (SS 07/2026, DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) from Sinokor Maritime at the same price i.e. USD 43,1 mill. Moreover, Maran Dry Management committed their \"Maran Innovation\" 171/2004 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 03/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at low-mid USD 13 mill basis prompt delivery. Remind you that back in April, the sister vessel \"Maran Pioneer\" 171/2004 Daewoo, Korea (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 16,6 mill. Star Bulk Carriers have sold their Kamsarmax \"Star Jennifer\" 82/2006 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 03/2026, DD 08/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) at USD 14,5 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Restinga\" 82/2006 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 09/2026, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in July at mid- high USD 13 mill. The Panamax \"Omicron Light\" 76/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold to Vietnamese buyers Hoanh Son Group at high USD 10 mill. The vessel was delivered to her new owners and renamed to \"Hoanh Son Universe\". Note that the sister vessel \"Magic Moon\" 76/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed a week ago at USD 11,8 mill. On the Supramax sector, Highland Maritime committed their \"NPS Mosa\" 53/2007 Iwagi, Japan (SS 06/2027, DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for USD 11,6 mill. In addition, India Cements committed their \"Chennai Selvam\" 52/2001 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 11/2026, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) at USD 6,5 mill, while the sister vessel \"New Lotus\" 52/2001 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 02/2026, DD 07/2024) was sold a week ago at USD 6,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Aframax \"Aegean Myth\" 115/2006 Samsung, Korea (SS 08/2026, DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) of Arcadia Shipmanagement was committed to Chinese interests at USD 37,5 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger \"P. Kikuma\" 115/2007 Samsung, Korea (SS 11/2027, DD 02/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 39,3 mill. Flynn Ventures have committed their MR2 \"Ocios Ioannis\" 47/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) for USD 25 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the \"UOG Helios\" 46/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 04/2024, DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at region USD 25,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid usd 9,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 12,000/15,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 13,000/17,000 pd. South African trips via North Coast South America into Japan were reported at the level of usd 19,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K. Continental trips via US East Coast into West Africa were fixed around usd 24,000/27,000 pd. Continental trips via East Coast Canada into China were reported at the level of usd 34,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Black Sea into Persian Gulf were fixed around usd 27,000/28,000 pd. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 15,500 pd basis delivery Japan for 5/7 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. East Coast Indian trips via Indonesia into China were fixed around usd 8,000/10,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 5,000/7,000 pd. West African trips into Baltic were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US East Coast were fixed around usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into US Gulf or South America were reported at the level of usd 9,000/12,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
